## Paired backend

This project is wired to talk to **{{#hasBackendArtifactId}}`{{backendArtifactId}}`{{/hasBackendArtifactId}}{{^hasBackendArtifactId}}a backend{{/hasBackendArtifactId}}** at `{{apiBaseUrl}}`.

- `vite.config.ts` proxies `/api/*` to `{{apiBaseUrl}}`, so with `VITE_API_BASE_URL` left empty the browser calls same-origin `/api/...` in dev and no CORS setup is needed.
- When `VITE_API_BASE_URL` is set in `.env.development`, the browser calls that origin directly and bypasses the proxy (the backend must then allow this origin).
- In production `nginx/nginx.conf` proxies `/api/` the same way, to the backend named by the `API_UPSTREAM` container env var.
- `.env.example` documents the override pattern for other environments.

Start the backend first, then run `dev` above.

